-- title:
--   Grouping column weights by slot and tag
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a counterexample to the duality conjecture for metric entropy. For every $a,b\ge1$ there are $n$ and a symmetric convex body $K\subset\mathbb R^n$ with $\log N(K,Q_n)>b\log N(Q_n^\circ,a^{-1}K^\circ)$. Here $Q_n=[-1,1]^n$ is the cube, $K^\circ=\{y:\langle x,y\rangle\le1\text{ for all }x\in K\}$ is the polar (so $Q_n^\circ$ is the $\ell_1$ ball), and $N(A,B)$ is the least number of translates of $B$ covering $A$. Let $\mu$ be weights on a finite set $Y$ of columns, $\alpha:Y\to K\cup\{\mathrm{none}\}$ an optional slot assignment, and $\tau:Y\to\mathcal T$ a tag.
--
--   1. **Grouped weight.**
--   $$
--   W(k,T)=\sum_{y:\ \alpha(y)=k,\ \tau(y)=T}\mu_y .
--   $$
--   2. **Use.** Any weighted sum $\sum_y\mu_yf(\alpha(y),\tau(y))$ over assigned columns equals $\sum_{k,T}W(k,T)f(k,T)$. So only the grouped weights indexed by slots and label sets need to be encoded.
